    <section id="about" class="container about">
      <h3>About</h3>
      <p>I'm Harjot Singh, a student at Thomas A. Edison High School who enjoys creative coding with CodeSkulptor and EarSketch. I focus on animation and audio projects.</p>
      <h4>My Growth as a Programmer</h4>
      <p>Programming is like problem-solving. Each project teaches me new challenges and how to break them down. Mistakes help me learn. Tools like CodeSkulptor, EarSketch, and HTML/CSS show creativity in code. I'm excited to keep building.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="projects" class="container projects">
      <h3>Projects</h3>
      <div class="project-grid">
        <article class="card" aria-labelledby="p1-title">
          <div class="card-image">
            <img src="https://github.com/Harjot478/HS_HTML-CSS-review/blob/main/html-css-project.png?raw=true" alt="Screenshot of the portfolio website" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px;">
          </div>
          <h4 id="p1-title">Holidays (draw) Animation Project</h4>
          <p class="project-meta"><strong>Type:</strong> Animation • <strong>Tools:</strong> CodeSkulptor</p>
          <p>A winter holiday scene where snowflakes fall continuously from the sky while ornaments change colors on the tree.</p>
              <p><strong>What I Learned:</strong> Learned to use loops for animations and real-time color updates. Timing is key for smooth effects. Testing catches bugs early.</p>
          <p><a href="https://py3.codeskulptor.org/#user310_b3c7SYk5aM33QeL.py" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View project →</a></p>
        </article>

        <article class="card" aria-labelledby="p2-title">
          <div class="card-image">
            <img src="IMG_0179.jpeg" alt="Image for Holidays Drawing Project" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px;">
          </div>
          <h4 id="p2-title">Holidays Drawing Project</h4>
          <p class="project-meta"><strong>Type:</strong> Portfolio / Tech Manual • <strong>Tools:</strong> CodeSkulptor</p>
              <p>In this assignment I was tasked with creating a snowman and a Christmas tree, a practice in shapes and layering.</p>
              <p><strong>What I Learned:</strong> Learned to break drawings into shapes like circles and rectangles. Organization and layering are important.</p>
          <p><a href="https://py3.codeskulptor.org/#user310_MRWGb391oFt5K2k.py" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View project →</a></p>
        </article>

        <article class="card" aria-labelledby="p3-title">
          <div class="card-image">
            <img src="Screenshot 2026-01-20 10.51.43 AM.png" alt="Image for Holiday Remix Challenge" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px;">
          </div>
          <h4 id="p3-title">Holiday Remix Challenge</h4>
          <p class="project-meta"><strong>Type:</strong> Sound • <strong>Tools:</strong> EarSketch</p>
          <p>Created a holiday-themed sound using EarSketch, focusing on rhythm and layering to evoke a festive mood.</p>
              <p><strong>What I Learned:</strong> Sound programming is creative. Layering tracks makes music interesting. Audio and visual programming share logic.</p>
          <p><a href="https://earsketch.gatech.edu/earsketch2/?sharing=aY5XjuSO4s-npxfcyWn7Hw" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Listen / Open →</a></p>
        </article>

        <article class="card" aria-labelledby="p4-title">
          <div class="card-image">
            <img src="Screenshot 2026-05-27 at 8.33.51 PM.png" alt="Screenshot of the Rainforest Game" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px;">
          </div>
          <h4 id="p4-title">Rainforest Game</h4>
          <p class="project-meta"><strong>Type:</strong> Game • <strong>Tools:</strong> Unity</p>
          <p>An educational game that combines entertainment with learning about environmental issues. Features levels with increasing difficulty, meaningful objectives, scoring systems, obstacles, and collectibles.</p>
              <p><strong>What I Learned:</strong> I learned how to combine entertainment with education by using gameplay to teach players about environmental issues. I also learned how to design levels with increasing difficulty, create meaningful objectives, and use features like scoring systems, obstacles, and collectibles to make the game more engaging and impactful.</p>
          <p><a href="https://play.unity.com/en/games/cee8c95d-8753-4f83-957c-6bb353afb3e5/rainforest-game" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Play game →</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="skills" class="container skills">
      <h3>Skills</h3>
      <ul class="skill-list">
        <li>HTML</li>
        <li>CSS</li>
        <li>JavaScript</li>
        <li>Creative</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <small>© Harjot Singh, <a href="https://github.com/Harjot478" aria-label="GitHub">GitHub</a> • <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/harjot-singh-a86337390" aria-label="LinkedIn">LinkedIn</a> • <a href="mailto:harjots2789@nycstudents.net">Email</a></small>
    </div>
  </footer>
  <script>
    (function(){
      const body = document.body;
      const btn = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
      try{
        const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
        if(stored === 'dark') body.classList.add('roblox-dark');
        else if(stored === 'light') body.classList.remove('roblox-dark');
      }catch(e){}
      if(btn){
        btn.addEventListener('click', function(){
          const isNowDark = body.classList.toggle('roblox-dark');
          try{ localStorage.setItem('theme', isNowDark ? 'dark' : 'light'); }catch(e){}
          btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', isNowDark ? 'true' : 'false');
        });
      }
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
